sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-gotcha-kcnh2a-filed-against-feature-not-gene> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "ZFIN holds zero phenotype rows for kcnh2a because the longfin phenotypes are filed against the chromosomal feature rather than against the gene, so a gene-keyed pipeline silently misses the best-known fin-overgrowth mutant; and the clone-autonomy experiment behind its sufficiency grade used human KCNH2, not the zebrafish gene" ;
    dct:description "Status: serendipitous methodological finding, established by inspection of the ZFIN files and the cited papers. The vetted genotype map never attached kcnh2a to any blueprint node, and the reason is a filing convention, not an absence of biology: in ZFIN the longfin phenotypes belong to the lof feature, while the gene kcnh2a has no phenotype row at all. Its only ZFIN gene-level records are wild-type expression rows on the generic terms fin and regenerating fin. Any pipeline that joins phenotypes to genes by gene identifier, as this thread's does, therefore misses the classic fin-overgrowth mutant entirely, and would report kcnh2a as unstudied in the fin. Second caveat on the same gene: the sufficiency grade on its chain rests partly on an experiment that overexpressed HUMAN KCNH2 in zebrafish fin mesenchyme (\"Upregulation of human KCNH2 in fin mesenchyme during development (ubi:hKCNH2;ubi:GFP) was sufficient to cause localized overgrowth of rays\", Daane 2021), so the sufficiency shown is of the human channel in a zebrafish fin, not of the zebrafish gene. Third: the full text of Stewart 2021, which carries the process step, could not be fetched (Europe PMC returned HTTP 500 for PMC8217709 and NCBI PMC reported that the publisher does not allow it), so every statement from it is abstract-only. What it does not establish: It does not establish that ZFIN is wrong: filing a phenotype against the feature is correct when the allele is a chromosomal rearrangement whose gene assignment came later. It does not show how many other genes are affected by the same convention; that was not counted. It does not weaken the longfin biology itself, only the chain of evidence tying it to the zebrafish gene. Pre-registration: none: a gotcha." ;
    delphi:context "Found while building the causal chains: the wing subagent could not locate a single ZFIN phenotype row for a gene with a famous fin phenotype. Chain grades for the gene: gene->molecular_function: mechanism; molecular_function->process: mechanism; process->cell_or_tissue_effect: sufficiency; cell_or_tissue_effect->phenotype: sufficiency." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-kcnh2a-filed-against-feature-not-gene> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-genotype-thread-claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-kcnh2a-filed-against-feature-not-gene> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "ZFIN row counts for kcnh2a and the provenance of its sufficiency grade" ;
    dct:description "Read from genotype/causal-chains.json, gene kcnh2a, and from the ZFIN bulk files in the thread's raw set." ;
    delphi:statisticalTest "Inspection: a search of ZFIN phenoGeneCleanData_fish.txt for the gene symbol and identifier, and of wildtype-expression_fish.txt for its expression rows; plus the fetched text of the two papers behind the chain. No statistical test." ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/zfin-bulk-downloads-2026-10-31> ;
    dct:source <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42623840/>, <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34061172/>, <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34534441/>, <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41728344/> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom sub:chains ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/genotype/data.json> .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42623840/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Functional characterization of zebrafish Kcnh2a splice variants reveals distinct gating properties." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Kume S 2026 Biochem Biophys Res Commun" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 42623840" , "doi:10.1016/j.bbrc.2026.154446" ;
    delphi:context "abstract only: the full text could not be fetched" ;
    rdfs:comment "In the present study, we cloned the full-length zebrafish kcnh2a-201 (z2a-201) and its splice variant, kcnh2a-202 (z2a-202), and examined their electrophysiological properties using two-electrode voltage-clamp recordings in Xenopus oocytes." .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34061172/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "longfin causes cis-ectopic expression of the kcnh2a ether-a-go-go K+ channel to autonomously prolong fin outgrowth." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Stewart S 2021 Development" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 34061172" , "doi:10.1242/dev.199384" ;
    delphi:context "abstract only: the full text could not be fetched" ;
    rdfs:comment "We show longfint2 chromosome 2 overexpresses the ether-a-go-go-related voltage-gated potassium channel kcnh2a." .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34534441/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Modulation of bioelectric cues in the evolution of flying fishes." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Daane JM 2021 Curr Biol" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 34534441" , "doi:10.1016/j.cub.2021.08.054" ;
    delphi:context "full text read" ;
    rdfs:comment "Thus, the chromosomal rearrangement in lof changes the regulation of the potassium channel kcnh2a, enhancing kcnh2a expression in the forming fin and is sufficient for increased fin size." .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41728344/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Increased diameter of arteries and veins in the caudal fins of Danio rerio longfin t2 fish is accompanied by fin overgrowth." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Lanni JS 2026 MicroPubl Biol" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 41728344" , "doi:10.17912/micropub.biology.002008" ;
    delphi:context "abstract only: the full text could not be fetched" ;
    rdfs:comment "Here we show that lof t2 fish contain significantly increased artery and vein diameters in the caudal fin as compared to wildtype fish." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-kcnh2a-filed-against-feature-not-gene> schema:additionalProperty sub:m0 .
  sub:m0 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "status" ; schema:value "serendipitous methodological finding, established by inspection of the ZFIN files and the cited papers" ; schema:description "status of this record in the words of AGENTS.md (supported, refuted, mixed, inconclusive, or a descriptive status)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-kcnh2a-filed-against-feature-not-gene> schema:additionalProperty sub:m1 .
  sub:m1 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "zfin_phenotype_rows_for_kcnh2a" ; schema:value "0"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "phenotype rows keyed to the gene in ZFIN" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-kcnh2a-filed-against-feature-not-gene> schema:additionalProperty sub:m2 .
  sub:m2 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "zfin_wildtype_expression_rows" ; schema:value "2"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "gene-level ZFIN records, both on generic fin terms" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-kcnh2a-filed-against-feature-not-gene> schema:additionalProperty sub:m3 .
  sub:m3 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "sufficiency_experiments_using_the_zebrafish_gene" ; schema:value "0"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "clone-autonomy overexpression experiments using zebrafish kcnh2a rather than human KCNH2 in the fetched sources" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-gotcha-kcnh2a-filed-against-feature-not-gene> schema:additionalProperty sub:m4 .
